<p>Our work explores how Large Language Models (LLMs) can enable more intuitive human–robot collaboration in manufacturing. In particular, we developed a framework that allows a human operator to use verbal guidance to teach a robot new assembly tasks, connecting natural-language instructions with executable robotic skills and trajectories.</p>

